{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nMCP tracker `claim` fails on the on-box server with:\n\n```\nno certified plan-review attestation (signature: foreign_key; this\nenvironment has no op-cert public key; it cannot certify any signature)\n```\n\nThe MCP container is KEY-LESS for op-cert signing.\n\n`rebar._opcert_signing.resolve` picks the op-cert key in this order:\n\n1. a context-local startup binding (`rebar._opcert_binding.current_binding`),\n2. the `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` env override,\n3. the `<tracker>/.opcert-key` genesis file.\n\nOn the live container none of the three yields a key:\n\n- `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` is UNSET,\n- `<tracker>/.opcert-key` is ABSENT (tracker is `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`),\n- the startup binding, composed by `mcp_server.compose_startup_opcert_binding`\n  from `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` + `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`, is threaded as a\n  ContextVar around serving (`rebar._mcp_health.run_mcp`) and is not observed on\n  the tool-call path that signs.\n\n`rebar.signing` states the consequence directly: a key-less environment can only\never report `unsigned` / `foreign_key`.\n\nThe Ed25519 key file IS already bind-mounted read-only at\n`/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` by BOTH launch paths (verified present, 411\nbytes, in the live container). Only the env var that points at it is missing.\n\n## Scope\n\nBoth launch paths are affected, not just one:\n\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` `mcp:` service mounts the key and sets\n  `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` and `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`, but NOT\n  `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`. (The `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` already in that file\n  belongs to the `opcert:` service, a different service.)\n- the `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` blue-green `mcp_run_new` `docker run` has\n  the same omission. This is the path that actually serves `/mcp`.\n\n`test_docker_run_matches_compose_mcp_service` pins docker-run/compose parity in\nthe compose-to-run direction, so fixing only the blue-green run would silently\ndiverge the two. Fix both, keeping compose the source of truth.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` in the compose\n`mcp:` service environment and as a matching `-e` flag on the blue-green\n`docker run`. The mount already exists, so no new secret, mount, or terraform\nchange is needed. The env override is thread- and context-independent, so unlike\nthe ContextVar binding it holds on every tool-call path.\n\n`REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` STAYS. It is load-bearing twice over: it populates\n`cfg.identity.signing_key` for authorship signatures, and it is one of the two\nrequired inputs to `compose_startup_opcert_binding` (absent it, the startup\nbinding is skipped entirely). This change adds a fallback beside it, it does not\nreplace it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The compose `mcp:` service environment sets\n      `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH: \"/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key\"`. Checked by\n      `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py -k compose_mcp_service`.\n- [ ] The blue-green `docker run` in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` passes\n      `-e REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`. Checked by\n      `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`.\n- [ ] A regression test asserts the blue-green `docker run` command line carries\n      that flag with that exact value, and turns RED when the flag is removed\n      (mutation-checked by deleting the flag and re-running\n      `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`).\n- [ ] `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` remains set on both launch paths. Checked by\n      `grep -n REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`.\n- [ ] The repo gates stay green: `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`, and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py` -- the real-subprocess\n  blue-green suite. It stubs the box binaries onto PATH, runs the shipped\n  `autodeploy.sh`, and asserts against the recorded `docker run` command line,\n  so the new assertion binds the shipped bash rather than a copy of it.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` -- the static on-box infra\n  contract, re-run to confirm the compose edit breaks nothing.\n- Mutation check: delete the `-e REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=...` line from\n  `mcp_run_new` and confirm the new test FAILS, then restore it and confirm it\n  passes. A test that stays green under that deletion is worthless and must be\n  rewritten.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`, and\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` for the repo gates.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo terraform. No new secret or mount. No change to the ContextVar startup\nbinding mechanism, which is a separate hardening question."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787941825120539001,"uuid":"e7aea11d-7a2f-417c-80af-e8ede69d7fb2"}